# Documentation conventions

## Feature specs (`specs/**/spec.md`)

Canonical feature delivery specs live under Spec Kit. Index: `specs/README.md`.

When **actively changing** a feature (Living Spec), you may align sections toward the Spec Kit template (`.specify/templates/spec-template.md`). Do **not** rewrite historical bodies to the template unless that feature is being changed.

Legacy-shaped specs (Objective / MVP scope / Acceptance criteria) are valid at rest:

- Objective
- MVP scope / Out of MVP scope
- Inputs (tables where helpful)
- Flow or logic (include at least one **Mermaid** diagram when the flow changes)
- Acceptance criteria
- Risks

Keep **Implementation status**: `planned` | `in_progress` | `done` (or equivalent).

New features: create via `/speckit-specify` (next number after the index).

## Investing non-feature docs (`investing/docs/`)

Architecture, guides, PRDs, requirements, backlog stay here — not under `specs/`.

- Record closed decisions in tables (see "Decisions made so far" in `investing/docs/architecture/architecture.md`).
- Cross-link Spec Kit feature paths (`specs/<###-slug>/spec.md`) from the architecture module table.
- Do not contradict a closed architecture decision without updating the architecture doc first.

## Language

All spec text must be in English.
